# GitHub App credentials, mounted only into the github-token service. Optional: a level without
# credentials can't issue tokens, and everything else works as before.
#
# Each access level in github-token/levels.json has its own variables, prefixed with the level's
# name in upper case. Give each level its own App, with only the permissions that level needs, and
# no webhook (Metadata is added automatically):
#   github_read: read-only Actions, Artifact metadata, Checks, Code quality, Commit statuses,
#                Contents, Deployments, Pull requests
#   github_pr:   read and write Contents and Pull requests. Never Workflows. Pushes are limited to
#                apollo/* branches only by the org rulesets described in README.md, so create those
#                before installing this App.
#
# The installation ID is the number at the end of the installation's settings URL
# (https://github.com/organizations/<org>/settings/installations/<id>).
# Private keys go on one line: base64 < your-app.private-key.pem | tr -d '\n'
GITHUB_READ_APP_ID=
GITHUB_READ_INSTALLATION_ID=
GITHUB_READ_PRIVATE_KEY_BASE64=
GITHUB_PR_APP_ID=
GITHUB_PR_INSTALLATION_ID=
GITHUB_PR_PRIVATE_KEY_BASE64=
